! Two aluminium atoms in an hcp cell, norm-conserving LDA, smeared: a metal whose
! atoms are **not inversion centres**. The site group is -6m2, and its mirror
! sigma_h takes d(eps_k)/du_z at k to minus itself at (kx, ky, -kz), so on a
! wedge that keeps one of the pair the Fermi level's shift per displacement,
! def = d e_F / d u, is a wedge sum of order 1e-2 Ry/bohr whose average over the
! group is zero. `ph.x` averages it (`sym_def`, `efermi_shift.f90`); the loop here
! used the raw value until AUDIT-2026-11-20b #12, and the E mode read 150.96
! cm^-1 on the wedge against 146.03 on the whole grid. Every committed metal
! before this one had its atoms at inversion centres (fcc aluminium), where the
! raw shift is zero and the defect could not show.
!
! Not a physical structure for aluminium: c/a ideal, a near the fcc
! nearest-neighbour distance, 12 Ry, a Gamma-centred 4x4x2 grid (8 points on the
! wedge, 32 without symmetry).
 &control
    calculation = 'scf'
 /
 &system
    ibrav = 4, celldm(1) = 5.35, celldm(3) = 1.633,
    nat = 2, ntyp = 1, ecutwfc = 12.0,
    occupations = 'smearing', smearing = 'marzari-vanderbilt', degauss = 0.05
 /
 &electrons
    conv_thr = 1.0d-12
 /
ATOMIC_SPECIES
 Al 26.98 Al.pz-vbc.UPF
ATOMIC_POSITIONS (crystal)
 Al 0.333333333333 0.666666666667 0.25
 Al 0.666666666667 0.333333333333 0.75
K_POINTS automatic
 4 4 2 0 0 0
